location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "900000"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "925929"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "925944"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "31800"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "31863"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "31969"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "32044"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "32115"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "32187"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "32268"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "32349"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "32430"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "32497"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "32570"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "32646"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "32728"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "32810"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "32920"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "33018"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "257904"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "303000"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "2014270"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "359400"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "2002000"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/121"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Basketball, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "25 July –  7 August 2021"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2116"} "Saitama Super Arena, Chūō-ku, Saitama, Saitama Prefecture, Japan"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19001250"} "143 from 12 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Round-robin pools advance teams to classification matches."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "All the games took place at Saitama Super Arena. There was a minor change in the format, as the last several Olympics had two groups of 6 teams each, with eight teams advancing to a knockout stage. In Tokyo the groups were changed into three groups of 4 teams each, again with eight teams entering the single elimination phase."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The United States had won gold in 2008, 2012, and 2016 but seemed more vulnerable in 2021. The COVID-19 pandemic had forced the NBA season to start later and finish only the week before the Olympics. With that late finish many of the best American players elected not to compete at the Olympics. In addition, in pre-Olympic games, both Nigeria and Australia defeated the USA men, and the United States’ Olympic dominance seemed in danger."] "\n\n" [:p {} "One other change was that long-time Duke coach " [:a {:href "/athletes/5000593"} "Mike Krzyzewski"] ", who had coached the United States’ team at the last three Olympics, had stepped down, with the NBA’s San Antonio Spurs coach " [:a {:href "/athletes/2303408"} "Gregg Popovich"] " now in charge. It was likely a minor change as Popovich was one of the greatest coaches in NBA annals."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Once in Tokyo, France defeated the United States in the first group match, 83-76, further inflaming their critics. France went on to win Group A, while the USA finished second but still advanced to the knockout rounds. The other groups were won by Australia and Slovenia, which was led by 2019 NBA Rookie of the Year " [:a {:href "/athletes/146558"} "Luka Dončić"] ", who scored 48 points again Argentina in their group match-up."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Sparked by " [:a {:href "/athletes/126091"} "Kevin Durant"] ", who would win his third gold medal, the USA won their quarter-final over Spain, 95-81 and then beat Australia quite comfortably in the semi-finals, seemingly getting stronger with each game. In the other half of the bracket, France defeated Italy and then Slovenia to earn a re-match with the Americans. The final was relatively close, but the United States was in charge the entire second half and finally won gold by 87-82. Australia defeated Slovenia, 107-93, to take the bronze medal, giving the Aussies their first Olympic medal in men’s basketball after four fourth-place finishes (1988, 1996, 2000, 2016)."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button420139", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button420139').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Scoring Average"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Time Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "TP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2-point Field Goals Made"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2-point Field Goals Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2-point Field Goals %"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3-point Field Goals Made"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3-point Field Goals Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3-point Field Goals %"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Total Field Goals", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "FG"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Total Field Goals %", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "FG%"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Free Throws", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "FT"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Free Throws %"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Offensive Rebounds", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "ORB"] [:th {:data-